.SH SYNOPSIS
.IP
.EX
#include \(dqserver.h\(dq

void debug_init(int rfd, int wfd);
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Initializes the per\-session debugger state.
Zeroes the entire debug state structure, then sets the client read and
write file descriptors, \f[CR]step_mode\f[R] to \f[CR]DBG_RUN\f[R], and
\f[CR]next_bp_id\f[R] to 1.
.PP
This function does \f[B]not\f[R] activate debug mode or register the
pre\-command hook.
The hook is registered lazily when the first breakpoint is added (via
\f[CR]debug_add_breakpoint()\f[R]) or when the client sends an explicit
\f[CR]enable\f[R] message (via \f[CR]debug_handle_message()\f[R]).
.SH PARAMETERS
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]rfd\f[R] \(em File descriptor for reading frames from the client
(used by \f[CR]debug_wait_for_resume()\f[R] to receive step/continue
commands while paused at a breakpoint).
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]wfd\f[R] \(em File descriptor for writing frames to the client
(used to send \f[CR]break_hit\f[R], \f[CR]breakpoints\f[R],
\f[CR]ast\f[R], and other debug event frames on \f[CR]CHAN_DEBUG\f[R]).
.SH RETURN VALUE
None.
.SH SEE ALSO
\f[CR]debug_cleanup\f[R](3), \f[CR]debug_add_breakpoint\f[R](3),
\f[CR]debug_handle_message\f[R](3)
.SH NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
Safe to call multiple times; each call resets all state including any
existing breakpoints (though it does not free them \(em call
\f[CR]debug_cleanup()\f[R] first if breakpoints may exist).
.IP \(bu 2
The debug state is process\-global, which is safe because bash\-server
uses a fork\-per\-session model.
.IP \(bu 2
Auto\-initialization also occurs in \f[CR]debug_handle_message()\f[R] on
first call, so explicit calls to \f[CR]debug_init()\f[R] are not
strictly required for the normal message\-driven flow.
